# Commits that changed how the code is written without changing what it does.
#
# `git blame` reads this only if you tell it to, once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub applies it automatically in its blame view.
#
# Two rules for adding a line. Full 40-character SHAs only — git ignores short ones without
# saying so. And say what the commit was, because a bare hash is unreviewable: nobody reading a
# pull request can tell a correct SHA from a wrong one, which is why
# `scripts/check-blame-ignore-revs.sh` checks in CI that each still resolves.

